            "pk": "18098098997105528",
            "text": "May 5–6, Almaty Hub will host a two-day Building Unicorns workshop with Uri Levine - entrepreneur, investor, and co-founder of Waze and Moovit.\n\nUri Levine’s approach is simple, yet rarely put into practice: “fall in love with the problem, not the solution”. This is how strong technology companies are born.\n\nParticipation in a workshop is a unique opportunity to get firsthand insights from a person who stands behind:\n- Waze - acquired by Google for $1.1 billion\n- Moovit - acquired by Intel for $1 billion\n\n📍 On May 5, an open workshop will be held for early-stage startups. Participants will explore:\n• The journey from an idea to the first stages of growth: how to turn an idea into a product\n• Business model and strategy\n• Common mistakes at the start\n\n📍 On May 6, a workshop will be held for startups at the scaling stage (participation is only by invitation). The workshop will focus on:\n• Growth management\n• Complex management decisions\n• In-depth case analysis\n\nJoin us for the event:\n📅 May 5\n🕖 11:00 AM – 5:00 PM\n📍 Almaty Hub, 24 Zenkov St. | 4th floor\n\nRegistration link is in the bio: @almaty.hub.02"
